{"source_key":"sha256-bb90e64262274e867b24503ac18d6d2f","record_index":104,"record_hash":"sha256:fea266ca828cae7b93e158834dc6dd422f6926ae61ce87f686b0d940f3c6c529","timestamp":"2026-09-07T11:58:22.416Z","kind":"message","source_event_kind":"codex:response_item:message","role":"assistant","text":"I found the main cause: each worktree gets a traversal goal to connect with the entrypoint. Until that connection is found, the walker ignores its soft budget—and keeps the entrypoint walking too. An old fork can therefore pull traversal far below the normal cutoff.\n\nThere’s also a display gap: the exclusion set contains projected stack commits, so it can miss the workspace merge commit itself. I tried running the focused tests, but Cargo stops before compilation because `crates/gitbutler-stack/Cargo.toml` is missing. The findings so far are from source inspection.","tool_name":null,"tool_input":null,"source_record":{"timestamp":"2026-09-07T11:58:22.416Z","ordinal":104,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"[REDACTED:entropy]","role":"assistant","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"[REDACTED:entropy]","create_time":1788782292.739311,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]},"phase":"commentary"}}}